## What does this PR do ?

Allows to starts a Kuzzle node without the cluster module.

Users might want to run Kuzzle in single node mode only and thus don't want the cluster (small) overhead with ID Card renewal.

![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4447392/150009331-79b5f063-9644-4633-9af0-704a692cd841.png)

### How should this be manually tested?

<details><summary>applications code</summary>

cluster-app.js
```
const { Backend } = require('./index');

const app = new Backend('cluster');

app.config.content.services.internalCache.node.host = 'redis';
app.config.content.services.memoryStorage.node.host = 'redis';
app.config.content.services.storageEngine.client.node = 'http://elasticsearch:9200';

app.start();
```

micro-service.js
```
const { Backend } = require('./index');

const app = new Backend('micro-service');

app.config.content.server.port = 7513;
app.config.content.services.internalCache.node.host = 'redis';
app.config.content.services.memoryStorage.node.host = 'redis';
app.config.content.services.storageEngine.client.node = 'http://elasticsearch:9200';
app.config.content.cluster.enabled = false;

app.start();
```

</details>

  - Step 1 : Run services: `kourou app:start-services`
  - Step 2 : Build Kuzzle: `npm run build`
  - Step 3 : Run the cluster node (you can run as many as you want) `docker run --network tmp_default -v /home/aschen/projets/kuzzleio/kuzzle:/var/app kuzzleio/kuzzle-runner node cluster.js`
  - Step 4 : Run the micro service node: `docker run --network tmp_default -v /home/aschen/projets/kuzzleio/kuzzle:/var/app kuzzleio/kuzzle-runner node micro-service.js`

